`// AmbientError indicates an error occurred after a resource has been
// received that should not modify the use of that resource but may be
// useful information about the ambient state of the XdsClient`

Mentioned this which is the language from gRFC

I think I already commented about this at some point in this PR. This section is super confusing and there is no need for this:
```
// After one has been passed to an
// LRS function, it must not be modified. A Config may be used; the LRS package
// will also not modify it.
```

Can we have the `NewXxx` function here as part of this PR so we know how this will be passed?

How about simplifying this with something like

// LoadStore stores loads reported to a single LRS server.
// Use multiple stores for multiple servers.

Following the same pattern of not using `onXxx` for callback names, can we name this `callbackProcessed` instead?

And the first line of this paragraph could be:
// The callbackProcessed parameter is a function to be invoked by ...

